I'll split the shell into three views.

## Plan

1. A `TitleRow` with the project switcher
2. A **sidebar** that follows the activity bar
3. The centre, which keeps one view per tab

The layout goes to `workspace.json` through the existing [`StateStore`](https://github.com/athasdev/athas):

```rust
pub trait StateStore {
    fn load(&self) -> Option<WorkspaceState>;
    fn save(&self, state: &WorkspaceState);
}
```

> Sessions keep their view alive while they exist, so a running agent keeps running.

